-
name: The Black Swan Crisis
slug: 2026-11-black-swan-soxs
date: 7 November 2026
time: 6:30 PM – 10:30 PM
venue: The Lounge, Preston Road Community Centre, Abingdon, OX14 5NR
location: SOXS Con
tagline: Geopolitics meets the unknown at SOXS Con.
eventUrl: https://www.soxsgamingday.org.uk/megagame-the-black-swan-crisis/
tickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/soxs-con-2026-tickets-1993770446075
ticketLabel: SOXS Con tickets
bookingNote: Buy admission to SOXS Con, then use the Bookaby link in your confirmation email to reserve a place in The Black Swan Crisis. Convention admission alone does not reserve your game place.
listImage: images/black-swan.jpg
bannerImage: images/black-swan.jpg
description: |
  International relief efforts, civil wars, political turmoil — the world is in crisis, and you will take on the role of a national or global leader trying to navigate it.

  …and then things get worse — maybe a zombie plague, maybe Atlantis rises from the ocean, or maybe aliens are discovered on Mars — all you can do is expect the unexpected.

  Can you work out what’s going on, and make the right decisions? And can you push your own agenda forward at the same time?

  The Black Swan Crisis is a narrative-focused game of geopolitics meeting the unknown. Deploy your limited resources wisely and creatively, cooperate or betray, and create a shared narrative that shapes the world’s future.
logisticsAfter: |
  This session is for 8–24 players and takes place in The Lounge during SOXS Con's evening session.

  **Age 18+ only.**

-
name: Crisis: Mars
slug: 2025-11-crisis-mars-soxs
date: 1 November 2025
time: 6:00 PM – 10:00 PM
venue: The Lounge, Preston Road Community Centre, Abingdon, OX14 5NR
location: SOXS Con
tagline: Negotiation and conflict on the edge of Martian independence.
eventUrl: https://www.soxsgamingday.org.uk/megagame-crisis-mars/
listImage: images/crisis-mars.png
bannerImage: images/crisis-mars.png
logisticsBefore: |
  This game ran in The Lounge during SOXS Con 2025's evening session, scheduled from 6:00 PM to 10:00 PM.

  **Age 18+ only.**
description: |
  The year is 2241 and humanity has colonised the inner solar system with space stations and mining in the asteroid belt, and a colony and terraforming project on Mars.

  In recent years a growing movement on Mars is pushing for independence from the Unified Nations of Earth and they have just gained a majority in the Martian senate. You will take the role of an actor on the edge of this brewing conflict. You will have limited opportunity to change its course but conflict gives you the chance to achieve your own goals.

  Crisis: Mars is a small 2.5 hour megagame for 12–18 players, played in small teams with an emphasis on negotiation and simple rules.

-
name: Den of Wolves: New Eden
slug: 2024-11-new-eden-soxs
date: 2 November 2024
time: 12:30 PM – 4:30 PM
venue: The Lounge, Preston Road Community Centre, Abingdon, OX14 5NR
location: SOXS Con
tagline: A survivor fleet searches for a new home, with enemies among them.
eventUrl: https://www.soxsgamingday.org.uk/mini-megagame-den-of-wolves-new-eden/
rules: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PKjoNIS_Dw6GU2YWpyH-MVd_jYqe09rh/view
listImage: images/new-eden.png
bannerImage: images/new-eden.png
logisticsBefore: |
  This game ran in The Lounge during the first session at SOXS Con 2024. Players were encouraged to read the rulebook before arriving.
description: |
  In this game you will play a member of a space fleet, survivors of a massive attack from the nation of Wolf – decimating and subjugating the other settled worlds. Together you will be trying to survive in space, flee further Wolf attacks and find a new home for your people – a New Eden.

  The game runs for 8 to 18 players over 3 to 4 hours, split into 8 turns. The game plays in real time, so managing your time and delegating tasks is an important part of the game.

  Each player will be assigned a role on one of the survivor fleet spaceships and must work together to succeed. Each ship represents a team of players and each comes from a different nation or colony from before the attack.

  Beware, however, Wolf planted agents throughout the colonies before the attack and it’s highly probable that some will be hiding amongst other players in the fleet.

